1. en-e kur lu₂ til₃-la-še₃ ŋeštug₂-ga-ni na-an-gub
#lem: en[lord]; kur[mountain(s)]; lu[person]; til[live (of a single person)]; ŋeštug[ear]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: Now the lord once decided to set off for the mountain where the man lives; 
#etcsl: line-id=1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 10; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 10; OB catalogue from Urim (U1), 0.2.03, line 14; OB catalogue from Urim (U2), 0.2.04, line 9

2. en {d}gilgameš₂-e kur lu₂ til₃-la-še₃ ŋeštug₂-ga-ni na-an-gub
#lem: en[lord]; Gilgameš[1]DN; kur[mountain(s)]; lu[person]; til[live (of a single person)]; ŋeštug[ear]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: Lord @wRN{Gilgameš} decided to set off for the mountain where the man lives. 
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. arad-da-ni en-ki-du₁₀-ra gu₃ mu-un-na-de₂-e
#lem: arad[slave]; Enkidu[1]PN; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#tr.en: He spoke to his slave @wPN{Enkidu}: 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. en-ki-du₁₀ murgu ŋuruš-e til₃-la saŋ til₃-le-bi-še₃ la-ba-ra-an-e₃-a
#lem: Enkidu[1]PN; murgu[shoulder]; ŋuruš[young adult male]; til[live (of a single person)]; saŋ[head]; til[complete]; e[leave]
#tr.en: @q[Gilgamec,Enkidu]{“@wPN{Enkidu}, since a man cannot pass beyond the final end of life, 
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. kur-ra ga-an-kur₉ mu-ŋu₁₀ ga-am₃-ŋar
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; kur[enter]; mu[name]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: I want to set off into the mountains, to establish my renown there. 
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. ki mu gub-bu-ba-am₃ mu-ŋu₁₀ ga-bi₂-ib-gub
#lem: ki[place]; mu[name]; gub[stand]; mu[name]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: Where renown can be established there, I will establish my renown; 
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. ki mu nu-gub-bu-ba-am₃ mu diŋir-re-e-ne ga-bi₂-ib-gub
#lem: ki[place]; mu[name]; gub[stand]; mu[name]; diŋir[deity]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: and where no renown can be established there, I shall establish the renown of the gods.”} 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. arad-da-ni en-ki-du₁₀-e inim mu-un-ni-ib-gi₄-gi₄
#lem: arad[slave]; Enkidu[1]PN; inim[word]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: His slave @wPN{Enkidu} answered him: @q[Enkidu,Gilgamec]{“My lord, 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. lugal-ŋu₁₀ tukum-bi ud-da kur-ra i-ni-in-ku₄-ku₄-de₃ {d}utu he₂-me-da-an-zu
#lem: lugal[king]; tukumbi[if]; ud[sun]; kur[mountain(s)]; kur[enter]; Utu[1]DN; zu[know]
#tr.en: if today you are going to set off into the mountains, @wDN{Utu} should know about it from us. 
#etcsl: line-id=9

@variants

#etcsl#ms 1 ms. adds 1 line:
